Actually, let me reconsider the whole thing. The task says "An overflow condition occurs when processing an ill-formed CGATS file." Let me look at the `InStringSymbol` function in the current source:

```c
void InStringSymbol(cmsIT8* it8)
{
    if (it8->ch == '\'' || it8->ch == '\"')
    {
        int sng;
        sng = it8->ch;
        NextCh(it8);
        while (it8->ch != sng) {
            if (it8->ch == '\n' || it8->ch == '\r') break;
            else {
                StringAppend(it8->str, (char)it8->ch);
                NextCh(it8);
            }
        }
        it8->sy = SSTRING;
        NextCh(it8);
    }
    ...
}
```

This uses `StringAppend` which grows dynamically. So no overflow here.

